From: Sebastian Matkovich <sebastian.matkovich@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 30 Oct 2026 20:10:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] linuxkpi 802.11: firmware power save (ifconfig wlan0
 powersave)

LinuxKPI's 802.11 left vif->cfg.ps false and IEEE80211_C_PMGT off
("Currently PS is hard coded off!"), so a driver with firmware power
save never got it: ath10k sets WMI_STA_PS_MODE_DISABLED as soon as its
vdev starts, and the WCN3990 keeps its receiver on between beacons.

Now, for drivers with SUPPORTS_PS, net80211 is told it can (C_PMGT), and
its powersave flag (ifconfig wlan0 powersave, IEEE80211_F_PMGTON, which
takes effect at the next association) becomes vif->cfg.ps with
BSS_CHANGED_PS once associated, as mac80211 enables power save, with
mac80211's default dynamic timeout of 100 ms; off again at the
disassociation. net80211's software sleep (C_SWSLEEP) stays off. Nothing
changes without the flag.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
--- a/sys/compat/linuxkpi/common/src/linux_80211.c	2026-10-30 20:01:05.461155053 +0100
+++ b/sys/compat/linuxkpi/common/src/linux_80211.c	2026-10-30 20:01:05.471103889 +0100
@@ -2124,6 +2124,11 @@
 		vif->cfg.assoc = false;
 		vif->cfg.aid = 0;
 		changed |= BSS_CHANGED_ASSOC;
+		/* power save only while associated, as mac80211 */
+		if (vif->cfg.ps) {
+			vif->cfg.ps = false;
+			changed |= BSS_CHANGED_PS;
+		}
 		IMPROVE();
 
 		lkpi_update_mcast_filter(lhw->ic);
@@ -2967,6 +2972,20 @@
 		vif->cfg.aid = IEEE80211_NODE_AID(ni);
 		bss_changed |= BSS_CHANGED_ASSOC;
 	}
+	/*
+	 * Power save as mac80211 enables it once associated: the driver's
+	 * (its firmware's) through vif->cfg.ps, when net80211's is asked
+	 * for (ifconfig wlan0 powersave: IEEE80211_F_PMGTON, which takes
+	 * effect at the next association) and the driver has it.
+	 */
+	if (ieee80211_hw_check(hw, SUPPORTS_PS) &&
+	    vif->cfg.ps != ((vap->iv_flags & IEEE80211_F_PMGTON) != 0)) {
+		vif->cfg.ps = (vap->iv_flags & IEEE80211_F_PMGTON) != 0;
+		/* mac80211's default; some firmware refuses 0 */
+		if (vif->cfg.ps && hw->conf.dynamic_ps_timeout == 0)
+			hw->conf.dynamic_ps_timeout = 100;
+		bss_changed |= BSS_CHANGED_PS;
+	}
 	/* We set SSID but this is not BSSID! */
 	vif->cfg.ssid_len = ni->ni_esslen;
 	memcpy(vif->cfg.ssid, ni->ni_essid, ni->ni_esslen);
@@ -6947,6 +6966,14 @@
 
 	lkpi_enable_hw_scan(lhw);
 
+	/*
+	 * Power save done by the driver (its firmware): net80211's
+	 * powersave flag goes to vif->cfg.ps (lkpi_sta_assoc_to_run);
+	 * net80211's own sleep handling (IEEE80211_C_SWSLEEP) stays off.
+	 */
+	if (ieee80211_hw_check(hw, SUPPORTS_PS))
+		ic->ic_caps |= IEEE80211_C_PMGT;
+
 	/* Does HW support Fragmentation offload? */
 	if (ieee80211_hw_check(hw, SUPPORTS_TX_FRAG))
 		ic->ic_flags_ext |= IEEE80211_FEXT_FRAG_OFFLOAD;
